firmwarekit-n72-2x-direct-iboot.patch: boot iPhone OS 2.x on the iPod touch (2nd gen) to the home screen without Apple's SecureROM (docs/reports/m2-timeline.md).

There are two problems:
  1. FirmwareKit's N72 recipe builds the whole SecureROM -> LLB in NOR -> iBoot chain for 2.x (boot_strategy bootrom)
     and writes no iBoot.bin. Apple's SecureROM (bootrom_240_4) is not in the IPSW and we only have a "b ." placeholder,
     so after reset the CPU sits at address 0 (measured: R15=0, black screen, nothing on the serial port).
  2. Entering iBoot directly reaches SpringBoard, but it stops at "Connect to iTunes": on first boot 2.x's lockdownd
     turns on BrickState, which on an iPod only clears once a paired host sets the time over USB (what iTunes does on
     connecting) (qemu-ios docs/ipod/from-ipsw.md, "2.1.1 home screen: lockdownd's brick state"). We have no USB host
     side (the qemu branch of usbmuxd, libimobiledevice).

Changes (N72Recipe.swift only):
  - 2.x also writes iBoot.bin (the decrypted iBoot from the IPSW) and the lock records boot_strategy iboot and
    direct_iboot true, entering iBoot directly as 3.x does. Measured: iBoot-385.49 reads the DeviceTree from NOR and
    loads the kernel as usual; the SHSH wrapping in NOR needs no change.
  - 2.x pre-writes -BrickState = false into private/var/root/Library/Lockdown/data_ark.plist on the volume (owned by
    root), as N45Recipe does for 1.x, so no USB host is needed.
3.x and later are unchanged. Waking from deep sleep still goes through the ROM and hangs as on 3.x (a known iPod touch
(2nd gen) issue).

Usage: clone the LightTouchMac sources at b06012fa4c (do not change upstream/), apply this patch, swift build FirmwareKit.
Based on samhenrigold/LightTouchMac b06012fa4c.
diff --git a/Packages/FirmwareKit/Sources/FirmwareKit/N72/N72Recipe.swift b/Packages/FirmwareKit/Sources/FirmwareKit/N72/N72Recipe.swift
